 "notes": "Official outcomes a to g are tested. Plotting in all four quadrants (a), drawing a line from its equation (b), drawing parallel and perpendicular lines (c, e), parallel lines have equal gradients (d), perpendicular gradients multiply to -1 (f), and straight-line graphs for fares, tariffs and bills, including where two charges are equal (g). The drawing outcomes (a, b, c, e) have no family: a typed answer cannot check a drawing, so they need paper or an on-screen plotting task; a teacher should decide how they are assessed. parallel-table-pick builds its options in code and is tied at family level.",
